cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use STORM in your research, please cite this software release and the associated STORM paper."
title: "STORM: RDMA-based Monte Carlo Transport for Distributed-Memory Particle Simulations"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-24
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/maormizrachi/STORM"
url: "https://github.com/maormizrachi/STORM"
abstract: >-
  STORM is an open-source Monte Carlo particle-transport library for
  distributed-memory simulations. It provides mesh-independent particle
  management, pluggable transport physics and boundary conditions, and
  scalable inter-rank particle transfer using one-sided RDMA through
  Open Fabrics Interfaces (libfabric), with an optimized two-sided MPI
  backend as a portable fallback.
keywords:
  - Monte Carlo transport
  - radiative transfer
  - RDMA
  - high-performance computing
  - distributed memory
  - MPI
  - libfabric
